          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+n-algebra"} Lie n-algebra
            that generalizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+geometry"} n-plectic geometry
            %em
              Poisson bracket
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantum+geometry"} higher prequantum geometry
          %p
            More discussion is
            %a{:href => "n-plectic+geometry#PoissonLInfinityAlgebras"} here
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+geometry"} n-plectic geometry
          %p
            Applied to the symplectic current (in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            theory,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Donder-Weyl+field+theory"} de Donder-Weyl field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
            (see there) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Throughout, Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            a natural number and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(X)
            a closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential (n+1)-form
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
            we may regard as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-n-plectic+manifold"} pre-n-plectic manifold
          %p
            We define two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            defined from this data and discuss their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %em
              Poisson bracket Lie
              = succeed "-albebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Rogers10"} Rogers 10
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#FRS13b"} FRS 13b
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#FRS13b"} FRS 13b
          #HamiltonianFormsAndVectorFields.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ham
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ham^{n-1}(X) \subset Vect(X) \oplus \Omega^{n-1}(X)
            %p
              for the subspace of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+fields"} vector fields
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential (n-1)-forms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              satisfying
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi v
                    %mi ω
                    %mo +
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota_v  \omega + \mathbf{d} J = 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              We call these the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  pairs of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+forms"} Hamiltonian forms
                  with their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+fields"} Hamiltonian vector fields
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#FRS13b"}> FRS 13b, def. 2.1.3
            )
          #PoissonBracketLienAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty(X,\omega)
              has as underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              the truncated and modified
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi d
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi Ham
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^0(X)
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}
                    \\Omega^1(X)
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}
                    \\cdots
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}
                    \\Omega^{n-2}(X)
                    \\stackrel{(0,\mathbf{d})}{\longrightarrow}
                    Ham^{n-1}(X)
            %p
              with the Hamiltonian pairs, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HamiltonianFormsAndVectorFields"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
              = succeed "-brackets" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_1(J) = \mathbf{d}J
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo ≥
                            %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                            %mo )
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mi k
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_{k \geq 2}(v_1 + J_1, \cdots, v_k + J_k) = - (-1)^{\left(k+1 \atop 2\right)} \iota_{v_1 \wedge \cdots \wedge v_k}\omega
                  \.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#FRS13b"}> FRS 13b, prop. 3.1.2
            )
          #PoissondgAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{A}
              be any
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              relative to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundle"} prequantum n-bundle
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLie
                      %mi Qu
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgLie_{Qu}(X,\overline{A})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
              (regarded as an
              = succeed "-algebra)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              is
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLie
                      %mi Qu
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi v
                    %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi Tot
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi v
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi d
                      %mi Tot
                    %mover
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgLie_{Qu}(X,\overline{A})^0 = \{v+ \overline{\theta}  \in Vect(X)\oplus Tot^{n-1}(\mathcal{U}, \Omega^\bullet) \;\vert\; \mathcal{L}_v \overline{A} = \mathbf{d}_{Tot}\overline{\theta}\}
              ;
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLie
                      %mi Qu
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Tot
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgLie_{Qu}(X,\overline{A})^{i \gt 0} = Tot^{n-1-i}(\mathcal{U},\Omega^\bullet)
            %p
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              given by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi d
                      %mi Tot
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}_{Tot}
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tot
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tot
              refers to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
              of the Cech-de Rham
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            %p The non-vanishing dg-Lie bracket on this complex are defined to be
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi θ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi θ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi θ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mn 2
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi θ
                            %mo ¯
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [v_1 + \overline{\theta}_1, v_2 + \overline{\theta}_2] = [v_1, v_2] + \mathcal{L}_{v_1}\overline{\theta}_2 - \mathcal{L}_{v_2}\overline{\theta}_1
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mover
                          %mi θ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo ,
                        %mover
                          %mi η
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi η
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mover
                          %mi θ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi v
                        %mover
                          %mi η
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [v+ \overline{\theta}, \overline{\eta}] = - [\eta, v + \overline{\theta}] = \mathcal{L}_v \overline{\eta}
                  \.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#FRS13b"}> FRS 13b, def./prop. 4.2.1
            )
          #ComparisonTheorem.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} homotopy theory of L-∞ algebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLie
                      %mi Qu
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f
                    \\colon
                    L_\infty(X,\omega)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    dgLie_{Qu}(X,\overline{A})
            %p
              between the
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoissonBracketLienAlgebra"}
              and def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoissondgAlgebra"}
              (in particular def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoissondgAlgebra"}
              does not depend on the choice of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{A}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
              satisfies
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo +
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi v
                      %mo −
                      %mi J
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi 𝒰
                      %mo +
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi v
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(v + J) = v - J|_{\mathcal{U}} + \sum_{i = 0}^n (-1)^i \iota_v A^{n-i}
                \.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#FRS13b"}> FRS 13b, theorem 4.2.2
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#the_extension_theorem The extension theorem
          #ExtensionTheorem.num_defn
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre+n-plectic+manifold"} pre n-plectic manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega_{n+1})
